LICENSE. It builds on, and runs, the following work under their own terms.

Engine
- vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Apache-2.0. The image is
  upstream vLLM's wheel for commit a0d7356b98, the fork's vLLM branch over it and
  the vllm-cmp170hx plugin, all from https://github.com/AlexBrandes/vllm, also
  Apache-2.0 (see that repository's NOTICE), on NVIDIA's CUDA 13.0 Ubuntu 24.04
  base image.
- The plugin's layout, startup guard and seam tooling are adapted from
  vllm-sm80 by Morrowmake (https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx),
  Apache-2.0.
- The threaded PLE row reader follows the approach of two community CMP 170HX
  projects:
  - polyuij42-del/qwen38-flash-next-w4a16-cmp170hx, MIT (copyright notice in
    licenses/polyuij42-del-qwen38-flash-next-w4a16-cmp170hx.LICENSE);
  - nguyenthimy2022kg-alt/Qwen-Flash-SM80-170HX, Apache-2.0.

Model
- Qwen3.8-Flash-Next by the Qwen team, under its license (copy in
  licenses/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next.LICENSE); the W4A16 checkpoint
  Intel/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-AutoRound was made with intel/auto-round
  (Apache-2.0). This repository ships no weights: download.sh fetches the
  checkpoint.

Benchmarks
- Speed tables use the sparkDash protocol (MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash, commit
  3e6d4ef, Apache-2.0); its prompts are used as data with attribution.
- GSM8K (OpenAI, MIT) as distributed with vLLM's tests/evals/gsm8k, and
  HumanEval (OpenAI, MIT).

